/target
/web/twiddlygems.wasm
/shots*
# The Archipelago tree, checked out to develop and test the apworld against.
# Not vendored: a pinned clone, the same one CI will make.
/vendor
/.venv
# Where the .apworld is zipped up, and the scratch copy of the world it is
# zipped from. The Python that makes up the world is tracked; this is only its
# wrapper.
/build
# The world's data, which is a transformation of src/progression.rs and nothing
# else. `make apdata` writes it, and everything that needs it builds it first.
/worlds/twiddlygems/data/
# The manifest Archipelago reads before it loads the world. Generated by the
# same pass for the same reason: the game it names has to be the one the engine
# names, and Archipelago's own packager refuses the build if the two disagree.
/worlds/twiddlygems/archipelago.json
# The licence the packaged world ships with, copied from the root by `make
# apdata`. The root one is the copy anybody edits; this is where it has to sit
# to end up inside the .apworld.
/worlds/twiddlygems/LICENSE
# Left behind by running the apworld's tests.
__pycache__/
